 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\n\nwwf\n\n60 -4------------------------------------ ,\nMeasured\nLoad Shape\n\na0 rqeonree       ag\n\n10 -\n\n06:08                             12:00                <~<\u2014__>                 24:08\n=            t= 15 mins\n\nExample for Real-Time Pricing\n\n\u00ae Anewprice every 15 minutes\n\n\u00ae Consumption within the agreed reference quantity (yellow) = agreed price\n\u00ae Consumption outsidethe agreedreference quantity (red) = spot price\n\nProcess Flow\n\nIS-U-EDM allows you to prepare for RTP billing. An internal interface transfers prepared RTP data to the IS-U billing component.\nUnlike conventional IS-U billing, RTP billing allows you to bill very small units of time (such as data from 15-minute intervals). These\nunits of time correspond to the time units of the interval data measured.\n\n1 Note\n\nYou can find further information about RTP billing in Customizing under |SAP Utilities > Energy Data Management >\nInterface to RTP Billing } General Information on the RTP Interface. 3\n\nFormulas\n\nFormulas define the calculations that take place when an RTP interface is executed. You allocate a formula to an RTP interface.\nWhen you choose a formula, you define input parameters to be supplied to the RTP interface as well as the output parameters\n\navailable.\n",
